---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — 챌린저와 그랜드마스터 사이. (/ladder-gap)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `/esports` 는 그랜드마스터를 **인원수 하나만** 쓴다. 같은 수집에 GM 의 LP·승률·판수가
 * 다 들어 있는데 안 쓰고 있었다. 층 **사이의 간격**이 통째로 안 쓰인 축이다.
 *
 * ── 기사와 이어진다 ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `/article/korea-challenger-win-rate` 가 「한국 챌린저 승률이 꼴찌인 것은 상대가 세다는 뜻」이라 썼다.
 * 이 지면은 그 **한 층 아래**를 보여 준다 — 한국은 상위 300명과 그 아래 700명의 차가 가장 작다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 나흘이다. 추세가 아니다 ─────────────────────────────────
 * 8/5 는 키 만료로 비었고 소급이 안 된다. **결측을 지면에 적는다.**
 * 우리가 말하는 것은 「추세」가 아니라 **순서가 나흘 내내 같다**는 것이다.
 *
 * ⛔ 일본은 챌린저 50명·GM 100명으로 다른 곳의 6분의 1이다. 숫자는 싣되 기대지 않는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않았다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-ladder-gap.json';

const TITLE = 'How thin is the top of the ladder?';
const DESC =
  'Korea’s top 300 League of Legends players win only 0.45 points more often than the 700 below them '
  + '— the narrowest gap of six regions, on all four days measured. Elsewhere it is one to two points.';

const kr = data.rows.find((r) => r.code === 'kr')!;
const 최대 = data.rows[data.rows.length - 1];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: data.day,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://developer.riotgames.com'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/ladder-gap">
  <h1>How thin is the top of the ladder?</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every ranked ladder has a top tier and a tier under it. The distance between them says how
    steep the climb is at the very top — and it is not the same distance everywhere.
    Collected {data.day} at {data.collectedAt.slice(11, 16)} KST.
  </p>
  {/* ⭐ 2026-08-22 — 날짜는 적혀 있었는데 「그날 수다」라는 말이 없었다. 날짜만 있으면 손님은
      오늘 수로 읽는다. 자(check-kcw-stale-stamp)가 이 칸을 지킨다 */}
  <p class="note">
    <strong>That is the day it was measured, and we are not collecting at the moment.</strong> Our
    developer key expires every 24 hours and production approval is still pending, so this is one
    dated day rather than a running series. A ladder cannot be measured backwards, so the days since
    are gone rather than pending.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Korea’s top 300 barely beat the 700 below them</h2>
    <div class="flip">
      <div>
        <span class="lab">Korea — gap between tiers</span>
        <span class="big">{kr.gap.toFixed(2)} pt</span>
        <span class="det">
          Challenger {kr.cWin}% against Grandmaster {kr.gWin}%. The narrowest of the six regions.
        </span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="lab">{최대.region} — the widest</span>
        <span class="big">{최대.gap.toFixed(2)} pt</span>
        <span class="det">
          {최대.cWin}% against {최대.gWin}% — more than four times Korea’s gap between the same two tiers.
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>All six, narrowest gap first</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Region</th><th>Gap</th>
            <th>Challenger win %</th><th>Grandmaster win %</th>
            <th>Players (C / GM)</th><th>Median LP gap</th><th>Games each (C / GM)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.rows.map((r) => (
            <tr class={r.code === 'kr' ? 'me' : ''}>
              <td class="nm">{r.region}</td>
              <td class="tot">{r.gap.toFixed(2)} pt</td>
              <td>{r.cWin}%</td><td>{r.gWin}%</td>
              <td>{r.cPlayers} / {r.gPlayers}</td>
              <td>{r.lpGap.toLocaleString()}</td>
              <td>{r.cGames} / {r.gGames}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      A tier’s win rate is set by the opponents it draws, not by the tier itself. A narrow gap means
      the players just below the top take nearly as many games off the field as the players at the
      top do — which is what a deep player base looks like from the inside.
      {' '}<a href="/article/korea-challenger-win-rate">The same argument, one tier up →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The gap, every day we have measured</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Percentage points. {data.days} days — this is not a trend, it is a check that the ordering holds.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Date</th>{data.regions.map((r) => <th>{r}</th>)}</tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.series.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{s.date}</td>
              {data.regions.map((r) => (
                <td class={r === 'Korea' ? 'tot' : ''}>
                  {(s as Record<string, number | null | string>)[r] ?? '—'}
                </td>
              ))}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Korea is narrowest on every one of the {data.days} days, and the ordering of all six does not
      change. <b>2026-08-05 is missing</b> — the collection key expired and a ladder cannot be
      reconstructed afterwards, so that day is simply gone rather than interpolated.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/ladder-gap" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Riot Games</b> — {data.source}. Collected once a day at 22:00 KST.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Japan is a sixth the size.</b> Its challenger tier holds {data.rows.find((r) => r.code === 'jp1')!.cPlayers} players
        against roughly 300 elsewhere, and grandmaster {data.rows.find((r) => r.code === 'jp1')!.gPlayers} against
        700. A narrower cut of a smaller population behaves differently, and its figure is printed
        without being leaned on.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Win rate is over the current ranked split</b>, including games against opponents outside
        either tier. It is not a challenger-versus-grandmaster figure.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>{data.privacy}</b>
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Four days is a snapshot.</b> Nothing here says a gap is widening or narrowing. What it says
        is that the six regions sit in the same order every day we looked.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.7rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; line-height: 1.4; }
  .sub { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .note { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .9rem 0 0; line-height: 1.6; }

  .flip { display: grid; gap: .8rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 34rem) { .flip { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .flip > div { background: var(--card); border-radius: 8px; padding: .9rem 1rem; }
  .lab { display: block; font-size: .76rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase;
         color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; }
  .big { display: block; font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 700; margin: .25rem 0 .35rem;
         letter-spacing: -.01em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .det { display: block; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .84rem; }
  th, td { padding: .45rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right;
           white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th { font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .03em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
       font-weight: 700; }
  th:first-child, td.nm { text-align: left; }
  td.tot { font-weight: 700; }
  /* 한국 줄만 배경으로 뗀다 — 이 지면의 주어이지 등수가 아니다 */
  tr.me td { background: var(--card); }

  .src ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .src li { margin: .45rem 0; }
  .src b { color: var(--ink); }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
